{
  "phase": 2,
  "title": "Project document and editing session separation",
  "createdAt": "2026-10-14T20:12:41.190Z",
  "implementation": [
    "Explicit version-1 ProjectDocument contract and a separate mutable ProjectSession; existing ProjectState model APIs remain compatible.",
    "Normal saves omit decoded records, store revisions, formats, trainer indexes, decoded text banks, generated documentation indexes and reconstructible runtime sources.",
    "Script drafts, verification bytes, pending entry mappings, custom UI, C-Gear work, animation authoring baselines and changelog history remain durable.",
    "Recovery snapshots preserve available resource data when the source cache is missing or belongs to a different project.",
    "Deserialized and parsed resource buffers transfer into a session without a second buffer copy; unchanged source placeholders share one empty typed array.",
    "w2anim source archives own bounded file buffers and parsed caches, instead of retaining an entire ROM through a view. Reconstructible archive source bytes are omitted from normal autosaves.",
    "Legacy saves load without eager rewriting unless their embedded source needs migration. Unsupported or failed restores preserve the saved document and show an application error instead of importing a clean replacement.",
    "Derived location refreshes no longer request autosave or mark ROM edits."
  ],
